diff --git a/docs/api/sections/notifications.md b/docs/api/sections/notifications.md
index 6bddff1..b493cb0 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/notifications.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/notifications.md
@@ -96,3 +96,37 @@ __Request:__
 __Response:__
 
 Returns `204 No Content` on success.
+
+## `POST /:account_slug/users/:user_id/push_subscriptions`
+
+Registers the browser push subscription for the current device. Whatever lands in that user's tray is also pushed to the device, with the same title and body, and opens the card it's about.
+
+The signed-in user can only register a subscription for their own user.
+
+| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
+|-----------|------|----------|-------------|
+| `endpoint` | string | Yes | Push service URL from the browser subscription |
+| `p256dh_key` | string | Yes | Client public key (`keys.p256dh`) |
+| `auth_key` | string | Yes | Client auth secret (`keys.auth`) |
+
+__Request:__
+
+```json
+{
+  "push_subscription": {
+    "endpoint": "https://fcm.googleapis.com/fcm/send/example",
+    "p256dh_key": "BASE64URL_PUBLIC_KEY",
+    "auth_key": "BASE64URL_AUTH_SECRET"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+__Response:__
+
+Returns `201 Created` the first time, and `200 OK` if the same device was already registered. The body contains the subscription `id` and `endpoint`.
+
+Sending pushes requires `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` on the server.
+
+## `DELETE /:account_slug/users/:user_id/push_subscriptions/:id`
+
+Removes a device subscription. Returns `204 No Content`.
